      "message": "Done! I've fixed the accent handling in the `slugify` function. Here's what was wrong and how I fixed it:\n\n**Problem:** The original code skipped all non-ASCII alphabetic characters with `elif ch.isalpha(): continue`, so accented characters like \"é\" were completely removed instead of being converted to their base form. This made \"café\" become \"caf\" instead of \"cafe\".\n\n**Solution:** \n1. Used `unicodedata.normalize('NFD', ...)` to decompose accented characters into their base character plus combining accent marks\n2. Skip combining marks (Unicode category 'Mn') so only the base character remains\n3. Keep all alphabetic characters (now including decomposed base characters)\n\n**Results:**\n- \"café\" → \"cafe\"\n- \"Café Au Lait\" → \"cafe-au-lait\"  \n- \"España\" → \"espana\"\n- All existing tests pass ✓",
